 Day 06 - Date & Time Functions and Nested IF

 Overview

In this session, I learned Excel Date & Time Functions and Nested IF statements to work with dates, calculate working days, and handle multiple conditions.

Topics Covered

1. Date & Time Functions

TODAY()
Returns the current date.

NOW()
Returns the current date and time.

DATEDIF()
Calculates the difference between two dates based on the specified unit.

Syntax:

DATEDIF(start_date, end_date, "unit")

EOMONTH()
Returns the last day of the month after adding a specified number of months.

Syntax:

EOMONTH(start_date, months)

NETWORKDAYS()
Calculates the number of working days between two dates, excluding weekends and optionally specified holidays.

Syntax:

NETWORKDAYS(start_date, end_date, [holidays])


2. Nested IF

Learned how to use multiple IF conditions to handle multiple possible outcomes.

*Layered Logic

Nested IF allows multiple conditions to be evaluated within a single formula.

Syntax:

IF(condition1, result1, IF(condition2, result2, "default"))

*Sequential Evaluation

Excel checks each condition in order.

- If a condition is TRUE, its corresponding result is returned.
- The remaining conditions are not evaluated.

Handling Multiple Outcomes

Used Nested IF to classify data and return different results based on multiple conditions.

